fail[2]: With only 7 in the set, `get_random` must return 7.
fail[3]: Removing a number that was never added returns `False`.
fail[4]: Once 3 is removed, only 4 is left, so `get_random` returns 4. If you moved the last number into 3's place, check that you also updated its stored position.
fail[5]: A number can come back after it was removed: `insert(9)` returns `True` again.
fail[6]: After 0 to 998 are removed, only 999 is left. If `get_random` returns anything else, a removed number is still in your list.
