fail[3]: The only pair adds up to 2, not 3.
fail[4]: After `add(0, 1)`, `nums2` is `[2, 1]`: 2 + 1 = 3 and 2 + 2 = 4, one pair each.
fail[5]: Two adds turn 3 into 7, and 1 + 7 = 8. Each `add` must change the count of the old value and of the new one.
fail[6]: `nums1` holds 30 copies of 1, and each total `t` from 1 to 19 is matched by the one number `t - 1` in `nums2`: 30 pairs each, so 19 × 30 = 570.
